# Movie Recommendation System - Project Rules

## 1. Development Environment

### 1.1 Python Environment

- Python 3.9+ required
- Use virtual environment (venv) for development
- All Python dependencies must be listed in `requirements.txt`
- Use pip for package management

### 1.2 Node.js Environment

- Node.js 16+ required
- Use npm for package management
- All frontend dependencies must be listed in `package.json`
- Use yarn as alternative package manager if needed

### 1.3 IDE Configuration

- Use Cursor IDE as primary development environment
- Configure ESLint and Prettier for code formatting
- Enable Python linting with flake8
- Use Git for version control

## 2. Project Structure

### 2.1 Backend (Django)

```
movie_recommendation/
├── core/                 # Core functionality and utilities
├── movies/              # Movie-related models and views
├── metadata/            # Genre, person, and crew information
├── users/               # User management and authentication
├── recommendations/     # Recommendation algorithms
└── api/                 # REST API endpoints
```

### 2.2 Frontend (React)

```
frontend/
├── src/
│   ├── components/      # Reusable UI components
│   ├── pages/          # Page components
│   ├── hooks/          # Custom React hooks
│   ├── store/          # Redux store
│   ├── api/            # API client and endpoints
│   └── utils/          # Utility functions
```

## 3. Code Standards

### 3.1 Python

- Follow PEP 8 style guide
- Use type hints for function parameters and return values
- Write docstrings for all functions and classes
- Maximum line length: 100 characters
- Use black for code formatting

### 3.2 JavaScript/React

- Follow ESLint rules
- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement proper prop types
- Use TypeScript for new components
- Follow React best practices

## 4. Database Standards

### 4.1 PostgreSQL

- Use migrations for all database changes
- Index frequently queried fields
- Implement proper foreign key constraints
- Use connection pooling
- Regular database backups

### 4.2 Elasticsearch

- Index movies, genres, and persons
- Implement proper mapping
- Regular index maintenance
- Backup index configurations

## 5. API Standards

### 5.1 REST API

- Use versioning (v1, v2, etc.)
- Implement proper error handling
- Use JWT for authentication
- Rate limiting implementation
- Proper documentation with Swagger/OpenAPI

### 5.2 API Response Format

```json
{
  "status": "success",
  "data": {},
  "message": "Optional message",
  "errors": []
}
```

## 6. Testing Standards

### 6.1 Backend Testing

- Unit tests for all models and services
- API endpoint tests
- Integration tests for recommendation algorithms
- Minimum 80% test coverage

### 6.2 Frontend Testing

- Component tests with React Testing Library
- Integration tests for user flows
- E2E tests for critical paths
- Performance testing

## 7. Security Standards

### 7.1 Authentication

- JWT-based authentication
- Secure password hashing
- Session management
- CSRF protection

### 7.2 Data Protection

- Encrypt sensitive user data
- Implement proper access controls
- Regular security audits
- Follow OWASP guidelines

## 8. Performance Standards

### 8.1 Backend

- Implement caching (Redis)
- Optimize database queries
- Use connection pooling
- Implement proper indexing

### 8.2 Frontend

- Code splitting
- Lazy loading
- Image optimization
- Bundle size optimization

## 9. Documentation

### 9.1 Code Documentation

- Inline comments for complex logic
- API documentation
- README files for each module
- Architecture diagrams

### 9.2 Project Documentation

- Setup instructions
- Deployment guide
- API documentation
- Troubleshooting guide

## 10. Deployment

### 10.1 Development

- Use Docker for development
- Local environment setup
- Development server configuration

### 10.2 Production

- Use Docker for deployment
- CI/CD pipeline
- Monitoring and logging
- Backup strategy

## 11. Git Workflow

### 11.1 Branching Strategy

- main: Production code
- develop: Development branch
- feature/\*: New features
- bugfix/\*: Bug fixes
- hotfix/\*: Urgent fixes

### 11.2 Commit Messages

- Follow conventional commits
- Clear and descriptive messages
- Reference issue numbers
- Separate subject and body

## 12. Code Review Process

### 12.1 Review Requirements

- At least one reviewer required
- All tests must pass
- Code style compliance
- Documentation updates

### 12.2 Review Checklist

- Code quality
- Security considerations
- Performance impact
- Test coverage
- Documentation

## 13. Monitoring and Logging

### 13.1 Application Monitoring

- Error tracking
- Performance monitoring
- User behavior analytics
- System health checks

### 13.2 Logging

- Structured logging
- Log levels
- Log rotation
- Log analysis

## 14. Maintenance

### 14.1 Regular Tasks

- Dependency updates
- Security patches
- Database optimization
- Performance monitoring

### 14.2 Documentation Updates

- Keep documentation current
- Update API documentation
- Maintain changelog
- Update setup guides
